records/thesis-analyst/2026-07-07/2026-07-07t16-10-11z-cms-medicaid-total-enrollment-2027-04/normalized_cells.json:16:    "resolutionRule": "Resolve to the first CMS-published national Total Medicaid and CHIP Enrollment count for the April 2027 reporting period in the preliminary Performance Indicator Data monthly snapshot or its underlying Data.Medicaid.gov dataset, using reporting_period 202704 and preliminary_or_updated = P. The ledger target resolves to CMS national Total Medicaid and CHIP Enrollment despite the cms.medicaid.total_enrollment series slug. Use the national total for the 50 states and DC, not a state row, weighted average, BHP count, T-MSIS separate CHIP table, updated vintage, or later revision. Convert whole persons to millions by dividing by 1,000,000 and round the resolved value to one decimal. The condition is satisfied only if the community-engagement compliance deadline is in force on its statutory schedule and no federal statutory or regulatory delay has been announced by 2027-03-31; the numeric forecast is evaluated only if that condition is satisfied. Ledger discrepancy note: this run verified the official monthly release vehicle and recent official snapshot release dates, but did not find a future-dated CMS April 2027 release placeholder; 2027-09-30 is retained as the canonical ledger deadline while the substantive resolver remains the first official print.",
records/thesis-analyst/2026-07-07/2026-07-07t16-10-11z-cms-medicaid-total-enrollment-2027-04/normalized_cells.json:64:        "text": "Framing and exact resolver: this is the CMS preliminary Performance Indicator Data national Total Medicaid and CHIP Enrollment count for April 2027, converted to millions. I treat the ledger target as resolving to CMS national Total Medicaid and CHIP Enrollment despite the cms.medicaid.total_enrollment slug; that is a ledger-label discrepancy, not an independent change to the target. The target is a national total for the 50 states and DC, not a weighted average, state row, BHP count, or T-MSIS separate CHIP variant. I use the fixed-vintage first monthly print and ignore later revisions."
